    "text": "Q: What is the value of the receiver window (rwnd) for host A if the receiver, host B, has a buffer size of 5000 bytes and 1000 bytes of received and unprocessed data? Solution [A} ———_/B / Seun The value of rwnd =5000 - 1000 =4000. | Host B can receive only 4000 bytes of data before overflowing its buffer. Host B advertises this value~ in its next segment to A. Lo Q: What ts the size of the window for host A if the value of nvnd is 3000 bytes and the value of cvnd is 3500 bytes? Solution The size of the window is the smaller of mvnd and cwnd, which ts 3000 bytes.",
